<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Tumalo Falls from Skyliner Sno-Park</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:276-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.031730" lon="-121.514972"><ele>1445.1</ele><name>Skyliner Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead th:skyliner-snow-play (OSM node 2898613043 Skyliners Trailhead parking); confidence: high; pdf_page: 278; book_elev_ft: 4800; quote: From near the sno-park, ski north down a hill (Novice rating)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.031112" lon="-121.519601"><ele>1448.6</ele><name>Skyliners Road / Bear Wallow Road junction</name><desc>source: OSM: west end of Skyliners Road way 5371804, start of Bear Wallow Road way 5371530; confidence: high; pdf_page: 102; quote: Meissner: follow the road ... 1/4 mile to where road #4601 turns downhill to the right and crosses Tumalo Creek</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.032192" lon="-121.521312"><ele>1442.9</ele><name>North end of the Tumalo Creek bridge (road 4603 gate)</name><desc>source: OSM: Bear Wallow Road bridge way 189478515 over Tumalo Creek; node where Tumalo Falls Road NF 4603 (way 279479047) leaves Forest Road 4601; confidence: high; pdf_page: 278; quote: to a bridge crossing Tumalo Creek, then turn left onto the 2.5-mile almost level road that parallels the creek</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.031904" lon="-121.566371"><ele>1517.8</ele><name>Tumalo Falls Trailhead (road end, bridge)</name><desc>source: OSM: west end of Tumalo Falls Road (way 5370497) across the road bridge way 279479046; Tumalo Falls Trailhead parking node 2388477431; confidence: high; pdf_page: 278; quote: A stand of tall firs appears at the head of the valley where you cross a bridge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.033941" lon="-121.566979"><ele>1546.0</ele><name>Tumalo Falls viewpoint</name><desc>source: OSM node 2837031779 Tumalo Falls Viewpoint; confidence: high; pdf_page: 278; quote: turn 100 yards uphill to the falls, climbing for best views</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Tumalo Falls from Skyliner Sno-Park</name><desc>1. Skyliner Sno-Park -&gt; Skyliners Road / Bear Wallow Road junction: osm (high), 0.24 mi | 2. Skyliners Road / Bear Wallow Road junction -&gt; North end of the Tumalo Creek bridge (road 4603 gate): osm (high), 0.11 mi | 3. North end of the Tumalo Creek bridge (road 4603 gate) -&gt; Tumalo Falls Trailhead (road end, bridge): osm (high), 2.44 mi | 4. Tumalo Falls Trailhead (road end, bridge) -&gt; Tumalo Falls viewpoint: straight (medium), 0.14 mi</desc>
